candidate_llama_3_2_1b_instruct:
The issue is due to the `ssl_client_certificate` directive in your nginx configuration. The `ssl_client_certificate` directive is used to specify the path to the client certificate file, but it does not automatically set the `Any Purpose` flag. To set the `Any Purpose` flag, you need to use the `ssl_certificate` directive instead, and specify the path to the client certificate file.

Try changing your nginx configuration to:
```nginx
ssl_certificate /path/to/ca_chain.pem;
ssl_certificate_key /path/to/client_key.pem;
ssl_client_certificate /path/to/ca_chain.pem;
ssl_verify_client on;
ssl_verify_depth 2;
```
This should resolve the `unsupported certificate purpose` error.

