```csharp
X509Certificate2 myCert = new X509Certificate2(certBuffer);
bool isValid = myCert.Verify(X509VerifyFlags.AllSignatures, RootCertificate.PublicKey, X509VerifyFlags.NoCheck, out: out bool);

if (isValid)
{
    Console.WriteLine("Signature is valid");
}
else
{
    Console.WriteLine("Signature is invalid");
}
```

This will return `true` if the signature is valid and `false` otherwise.

