candidate_qwen3_32b:
Yes, the `X-Forwarded-Proto` header can be altered by an attacker, making it unreliable for security decisions. On Heroku, your app is behind a trusted load balancer, so you can safely rely on the `req.secure` property in Express, which checks the connection to the load balancer. Heroku terminates SSL at the load balancer and sets `req.secure` to `true` for HTTPS requests. To securely redirect HTTP to HTTPS, use:

```javascript
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  if (!req.secure) {
    return res.redirect("https://" + req.headers.host + req.url);
  }
  next();
});
```

